WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.510 --> 00:00:10.210
Back in October when I released my 94 Things
You Missed in IT, I theorized that Henry Bowers

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:14.750
may have killed his friends, Victor and Belch,
on the way from his house to the final showdown

00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:16.200
at 29 Neibolt.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:20.200
My reasoning behind the theory was that Henry
watches the tv show seen around Derry where

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:25.110
Pennywise encourages him to “Kill Them All”,
then kills his father.

00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:30.000
When we next see him at the 29 Neibolt house,
he pulls up in Belch’s car with more blood

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.440
on him than before.

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:34.980
So I thought maybe there was a deleted scene
involving Henry killing his friends and stealing

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:35.980
the car.

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:39.050
I declared that we’d have to wait for the
Blu-Ray to come out to see if I was right.

00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:41.040
So fast forward to today.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:45.190
At the time of me making this video, the Blu-Ray
still isn’t out in my country, but it has

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:49.370
been released in Australia and one of my fans
was nice enough to give me a heads up.

00:00:49.370 --> 00:00:53.840
The clip has only surfaced on Instagram so
far, so please excuse the quality, but let’s

00:00:53.840 --> 00:01:19.230
roll it.

00:01:19.230 --> 00:01:21.510
So it looks like I was spot on with the theory.

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:24.480
But what implications does this have for the
upcoming sequel?

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:28.020
In the book, Belch and Victor die not long
after, at the hands of IT.

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:32.180
In the adult portion, Pennywise exhibits the
forms of both Victor and Belch to help break

00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:33.590
Henry out of prison.

00:01:33.590 --> 00:01:36.960
Henry apologizes for leaving them to die in
the sewers all those years ago.

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:41.430
As of right now, we don’t even know if Henry
survives the fall into that well in the Neibolt

00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:46.180
basement, but if he does live, it’s safe
to say that Victor and Belch probably won’t

00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:49.020
be the forms used by IT to break him out of
prison.

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:51.540
That would be one awkward car ride.

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:55.230
If Henry doesn’t live, then with all four
bullies out of the picture now, who is going

00:01:55.230 --> 00:01:58.220
to be the new scapegoat for the killings that
took place that summer?

00:01:58.220 --> 00:02:01.880
Let me know your ideas in the comments, and
also let me know if you think this deleted

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:03.940
scene should have been removed or not.

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:08.390
And I know what you’re thinking -- CZ how
can I get myself some of that stylish Float.

00:02:08.390 --> 00:02:09.390
Merchandise.

00:02:09.390 --> 00:02:12.870
For that, you’ll want to head over to the
new CZsWorld Merch Store.

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:18.530
I’ll leave a link in the description.

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:23.319
But most importantly remember to subscribe
to CZsWorld for new horrors every week, ring

00:02:23.319 --> 00:02:26.930
the deathbell for notifications and I’ll
see you in the next one.

00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:29.180
Assuming we both survive.

